      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, that's definitely more \"user-centric\" in terms of the language, but honestly, the wording is getting a bit heavy and unnatural. \"Relief Needed for Best Effort Users\"? that sounds like a corporate memo, not a summary of what people are actually saying on social media.\n\nlook, i get that you're trying to hit that metric, but it's starting to feel like you're just forcing the words in. can you do one more pass? i need it to be high-scoring for the dashboard, but let's keep it actually readable. try to weave the user/customer/people perspective in more naturally so it doesn't look like you're just trying to hack the count. just make it a really strong, high-scoring summary.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
